==English==

===Etymology===
A [[reverse]] [[spelling]] of ''[[palindrome|palindromes]]''. "Semordnilap," according to author O.V. Michaelsen, was probably first used by recreational linguist [[w:Dmitri Borgmann|Dmitri Borgmann]], cited by Martin Gardner in the revised edition of C. C. Bombaugh's ''Oddities and Curiosities of Words and Literature'' (1961) [http://books.google.com/books?id=f4kNAQAAIAAJ&q=borgmann]. The underlying concept (but not the term) is found at least as far back as [[w:Lewis Carroll|Lewis Carroll]]'s ''Sylvie and Bruno'' (1889).

